    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0285" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/7–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-02T18:00:00-04:00">August 2, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Dept transmitted substance Urtels 385 and 386<anchor n="17" xml:id="d264-f1"
                    /> to the Secretary of State at Potsdam for consideration.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile, suggestion urtel 395 July 28 has been communicated to OWI which
                    indicates it will include in its Voice of America Broadcasts in Bulgarian
                    substance Petkov’s letter with expressions of approval by press or other private
                    sources in this country of desire for democratic procedures evidenced
                    therein.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
